{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "qubit-superposition-lesson",
  "title": "What is a Quantum Qubit?",
  "description": "Comprehensive exploration of quantum superposition, Dirac bra-ket notation, and probability amplitudes.",
  "concepts": ["qubit", "superposition", "probability-amplitudes"],
  "misconceptions": ["superposition-not-mixture", "measurement-deterministic"],
  "defaults": {
    "duration": 1.5,
    "color": "#F8FAFC"
  },
  "actions": [
    {
      "type": "WRITE",
      "id": "qubit-title",
      "text": "THE QUANTUM QUBIT & SUPERPOSITION",
      "x": 260,
      "y": 80,
      "duration": 1.6,
      "style": {
        "fontSize": 34,
        "fontWeight": "bold",
        "color": "#A78BFA"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "UNDERLINE",
      "id": "ul-qubit-title",
      "x": 260,
      "y": 120,
      "width": 760,
      "color": "#7C3AED"
    },
    {
      "type": "NARRATE",
      "text": "Unlike a classical bit, a quantum bit or qubit can exist in a linear combination of both state zero and state one simultaneously.",
      "duration": 5.5
    },
    {
      "type": "CAPTION",
      "id": "cap-qubit-intro",
      "text": "A qubit uses quantum mechanical principles: Superposition and Phase."
    },
    {
      "type": "WRITE",
      "id": "ket-heading",
      "text": "1. Dirac Ket Notation & State Vector:",
      "x": 140,
      "y": 170,
      "duration": 1.2,
      "style": {
        "fontSize": 24,
        "fontWeight": "600",
        "color": "#E2E8F0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "MATH",
      "id": "math-statevector",
      "expression": "|\\psi\\rangle = \\alpha |0\\rangle + \\beta |1\\rangle \\quad (\\alpha, \\beta \\in \\mathbb{C})",
      "x": 140,
      "y": 220,
      "duration": 1.8,
      "style": {
        "scale": 1.3,
        "fontSize": 24,
        "color": "#F5C842"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "HIGHLIGHT",
      "id": "hl-statevector",
      "x": 130,
      "y": 210,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 55,
      "color": "rgba(245, 200, 66, 0.2)"
    },
    {
      "type": "NARRATE",
      "text": "The coefficients alpha and beta are complex probability amplitudes representing the quantum state.",
      "duration": 4.8
    },
    {
      "type": "WRITE",
      "id": "norm-heading",
      "text": "2. Normalization Constraint (Total Probability = 100%):",
      "x": 140,
      "y": 310,
      "duration": 1.2,
      "style": {
        "fontSize": 24,
        "fontWeight": "600",
        "color": "#E2E8F0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "MATH",
      "id": "math-normalization",
      "expression": "|\\alpha|^2 + |\\beta|^2 = 1 \\implies P(0) = |\\alpha|^2, \\quad P(1) = |\\beta|^2",
      "x": 140,
      "y": 360,
      "duration": 1.8,
      "style": {
        "scale": 1.25,
        "fontSize": 24,
        "color": "#38BDF8"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "NARRATE",
      "text": "By the Born rule, the squared magnitude of alpha gives the probability of measuring zero, and beta squared gives the probability of measuring one.",
      "duration": 5.8
    },
    {
      "type": "DRAW",
      "id": "circle-bloch-preview",
      "shape": "circle",
      "cx": 880,
      "cy": 300,
      "r": 70,
      "filled": true,
      "duration": 1.2,
      "style": {
        "color": "#38BDF8",
        "strokeWidth": 2.5
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "DRAW",
      "id": "arrow-state-vector",
      "shape": "arrow",
      "x1": 880,
      "y1": 300,
      "x2": 930,
      "y2": 250,
      "arrowSize": 14,
      "duration": 1.0,
      "style": {
        "color": "#F5C842",
        "strokeWidth": 3.0
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WRITE",
      "id": "label-bloch-state",
      "text": "|ψ⟩ on Bloch Sphere",
      "x": 800,
      "y": 390,
      "duration": 1.0,
      "style": {
        "fontSize": 18,
        "color": "#CBD5E1"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "NARRATE",
      "text": "Geometrically, any single qubit pure state lives on the surface of the three-dimensional Bloch Sphere.",
      "duration": 4.5
    },
    {
      "type": "PAUSE",
      "duration": 1.5
    }
  ]
}
